{
  "about": "#691: a multi-part design drawn part by part, each part in its own colour. The companion writes current.parts (and each sealed version's result.parts) when the printer MCP meshes a 3MF's parts (counterpart/1 part-mesh tool, services/printer-handoff/src/model-parts.ts): [{id, name?, colour?, plate?, mesh}], mesh a project path to that part's STL in its object's frame (millimetres), colour #RRGGBB (the MCP's, else the pass's declared colour for its filament), plate the 0-based plate in a designer's kit. Without parts (an MCP without the tool, a one-colour model) nothing changes: the stage turns the merged mesh (mergedMesh, or the STL model) in the neutral material, as today. Every client (CounterpartKit, Android, Linux) reads each case: draw is what the stage turns for the design shown, in order, each mesh with its colour, or \"neutral\" for none. A designer's kit draws only the chosen plate's parts (publishedSelection.plateIndex); parts with no plate are on every plate. The companion's own test (services/companion/tests/objects-parts.test.mjs) writes the first two cases' records.",
